lumn of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is \n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+2y+3z &=0 \\\\ 2x+0y+3z &=2 \\\\ 2x+3y+0z &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain: \n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z &=0 \\\\ 2x+3z &=2 \\\\ 2x+3y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.$$" 13194139535650 17592186045443 true] [17592186287986 1074 "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\\begin{cases}4x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x-0y+2z=6 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{2}y+6z=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{cases}$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain \n\n$$\\begin{cases}4x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x+2z=6 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{2}y+6z=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{cases}$$" 13194139535650 17592186045443 false] [17592186287986 1074 "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$, $y$, and $z,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+y+z &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x-0y+2z &=6 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{2}y+6z &=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.$$\n\nBy simplifying, we obtain \n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+y+z &=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x+2z &=6 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{2}y+6z &=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.$$" 13194139535650 17592186045443 true] [17592186336441 1080 "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y &=1 \\\\ -2x-3y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right." 13194139535650 17592186045443 true] [1759218